summary.value:
The three reviewers are concerned about:
- unclear positioning;
- lack of baselines comparing to established methods; 
- weak treatment of the back projection step from relaxed to discrete parameters; 
- limited scope restricted to linear elastic FEM with spherical inclusions; 
- computational scalability, particularly for non-linear problems;
- statistical robustness with single training runs; 
- notation/clarity.

reviewer_concerns.value:
The authors have attempted to address the following concerns:
- Positioning: Revised to address ill-posedness vs. non-differentiability distinction.
- Baseline comparisons: Added Bayesian optimization and conditional diffusion model comparisons;
- Back projection analysis: Additional detailed analysis added to supplementary Section B;
- Gradient scaling sensitivity: Analysis added to supplementary Section D;
- Runtime analysis: Detailed breakdown added to supplementary Section F;
- Statistical robustness: Results now aggregated over 3 training seeds with standard deviations reported;
- Notation/clarity: Revised ambiguous terminology and notation;

Outstanding concerns:
- Performance degradation at extreme bulk moduli remains unexplained methodologically (attributed to data limitations);
- Computational bottleneck for non-linear FEM acknowledged but unresolved;
- Limited experimental scope to linear elastic problems persists;
- The method underperforms baselines for high target bulk moduli -> questions about practical utility;
- Connection to OED literature added but advantage over simpler gradient-based methods remains weakly demonstrated.
